Subject: [PATCH 09/10] fix: the answer fits above the fold without shrinking
 anything that matters
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Measured, not estimated: the three states were rendered with the compiled
stylesheet inside a real 375-wide frame in headless Chromium, and the
element that answers "is anything waiting for me?" was measured against the
667-pixel goal.

  attention  the call to action ends at 576
  calm       the sentence ends at 394
  degraded   the sentence ends at 405

No horizontal overflow at 320, 375, 414 or 768.

Getting there spent chrome, in the order the plan set: no bottom bar with
two sections, a shorter header, less vertical breathing in the opening and
in the slab on phones only. Nothing was taken from font size, touch target,
contrast or semantics — the goal never justifies a regression there.

The degraded heading dropped a step in the type scale. It was the loudest
text on the screen, which is the wrong tone for a block that reports a
failed read: it is less important than a real pending item, and shouting
louder than one is alarm.

Tests cover what the measurement cannot: one h1 and no level skipped, a
56-pixel full-width call to action, secondary rows that keep a touch
target, every stage announcing its state in words rather than colour, the
numeral hidden from screen readers with the sentence carrying the meaning,
no alert role and no live region anywhere, and no danger colour on the
degraded block.

